\section{Conclusion and Future Works}
We introduce Protap, a unified benchmark that brings together general-purpose pretraining architectures and domain-specific models to evaluate five key protein modeling applications under a standard, reproducible framework. 
Our extensive experiments indicate that no single model or pretraining objective can outperform all others across applications. The architecture and training strategy must be chosen based on the specific characteristics of each task. 
There are two directions that need further investigation: (i) We will further explore the scaling laws that govern how model capacity and pretraining data volume translate into downstream gains. 
(ii) We will extend Protap to holistically cover protein design tasks, e.g., peptide design, enzyme design. 


