$$with $z=-2(3^{-1})$ y $w=-3^{-1}$. As a result, up to automorphism of $H_2$, we can assume $g_1\in \langle A, B, S, R\rangle.$ Further, we can assume $g_1=S$ and therefore $\Theta$ is $H_2$-equivalent to $$(S, A^i B^j RC, (SA^i B^j RC)^{-1}) \mbox{ or } (S, A^i B^j R^2C, (SA^i B^j R^2C)^{-1})$$ Now,  as in Lemma \ref{Z11}, we can conclude that $\Theta$ is $H_2$-equivalent to $\Theta_2=(S, ARC, BSRC).$ 
\end{proof}

