 \begin{proof}[Proposition~{\rm \ref{prop:A0}}]
 Let us prove that 
$ A_0=2\zeta(3) $. From~(\ref{eq:ident1}) we have %% obtain that
   $$ A_0=\sum_{k\ge 1}  \sum_{m\ge 1} \frac{1}{k\cdot m\cdot (k+m)}. $$
   Then we derive that
   \begin{eqnarray*}
       \sum_{k\ge 1}  \sum_{m\ge 1} \frac{1}{k\cdot m\cdot (k+m)} &=&
