\section{Measurement description}
To characterize the MZIs, an automated test setup \cite{ref2,ref6} with automated control software written in Python was used \cite{ref3}.  An Agilent 81600B tunable laser was used as the input source and Agilent 81635A optical power sensors as the output detectors. The wavelength was swept from 1500 to 1600 \si{nm} in 10 \si{pm} steps.  A polarization maintaining (PM) fibre was used to maintain the polarization state of the light, to couple the TE polarization into the grating couplers \cite{ref4}.  A 90$^\circ$ rotation was used to inject light into the TM grating couplers \cite{ref4}.  A polarization maintaining fibre array was used to couple light in/out of the chip \cite{ref5}.

