When analyzing responses to sustainability relevance, a notable difference emerges between the groups. Base group members tended to classify posts as sustainability-relevant (``Yes'') more frequently, while F group ones were more inclined to mark posts as not relevant (``No''). This suggests that the F group may adopt a more conservative or selective perspective on sustainability relevance than the B group.% All in all, these observations may indicate that F group participants have a higher level of certainty but apply a stricter criterion when evaluating sustainability relevance. This distinction could reflect differences in interpretation or stricter standards in the F group compared to the B ones. However, further statistical analysis is needed to confirm the significance of these findings.
