The most appropriate statistical test for this scenario, with minimal assumptions and mode as its statistic, is the permutation test with 1,000 permutations~\cite{marozzi2004some} and~\cite{holt2023permutation}. Using mode as the statistic, the test yields a p-value of \textbf{0.001}, indicating sufficient statistical power to conclude that group F perceives usefulness significantly higher than group B.
