\section{Rationality Properties of individual LLM Forecasts}
In addition to analyzing the pricing behavior of LLMs, we were also interested in how these models generate forecasts for future price period, allowing us to assess not only the rationality of their forecasts—whether they align with fundamental valuation principles—but also whether the LLMs themselves behave rationally in response to their own expectations. This dual analysis helps us understand whether LLMs internalize consistent pricing logic and whether their trading behavior reflects an economically rational response to their own forecasts.

