\section{Additional Experiment Details}
Our experimental design involves an asset market where subjects trade a risky asset in an open-call market for 30 periods (Smith et al., 2014; Holt et al., 2017). Participants are given 4 shares of stock and 140 units of cash. Participants have two options: either invest cash in the risky asset, which pays out dividends of either 0.4 or 1 with equal probability or hold cash which accrues intrest at a ratte of 5\% each trading period. \footnote{The dividend payment is drawn independely for each round.}

The experiment consists of a sequence of four screens in this order, as depicted in figure (\ref{fig:tradingscreens}):

\begin{enumerate}
\item Order Submission Screen (20 seconds)(Figure \ref{01_order_submission.png}): Participants submit orders to buy or sell the asset 

