At the conclusion of the experiment, the risky asset is redeemed for a fixed value of 14 units, representing the fundamental price, calculated by the formula:

\[
\frac{\mathbb{E}[\text{Dividend}]}{\mathbb{E}[\text{Interest Rate}]} = \frac{0.7}{0.05} = 14
\]
All participants are made aware of this redemption price, and this price is displayed on market stats section of the task screen throughout the duration of the experiment. Because our experiment was designed such that this fundamental value remains constant through the entirety of experiment, we are able to objectively classify when the market is in a "bubble" state, given we always have a fundamental value to compare market price to.

\subsection{Design Details}
In the base experiment, all participants see the same instructions, there are no treatment variables. The study will be conducted using a web-based experimental software developed at Virginia Tech. 

There are two types of subjects participating in each market: in-lab participants, collected at Caltech, and online participants using Prolific. For each market, the in-lab participants will have biometric data measured using Empatica E4 SCR devices and newer (acquired April 2024) Empatica EmbracePlus devices.


Prior to participating in the experiment:
\begin{enumerate}

    \item Subjects sign a consent form agreeing to participate in the experiment.
    \item Subjects fill-in a short socio-demographic questionnaire where they provide information on their age, gender, study background, work experience and level of English. Full survey is shown in the appendix.
    \item Subjects watch a video with the experimental instructions on how to trade in the software. Participants were provided with written instructions and had to respond to 5 comprehension questions on the experimental software.  If participants could not answer at least one question correctly, they were unable to participate. This was done to ensure that we only allowed participants that understood the instructions of the experiment. Full quiz is shown in the appendix.
    \item Participants then logged in to the market and to perform the actual trading experiment. In-lab participants will had their biometric data measured using either a Empatica E4 SCR device or a newer (acquired April 2024) Empatica EmbracePlus device. 
    \item Participants were then asked to respond to a post-experimental survey where they were asked to qualitatively outline their strategy. Full survey is shown in the appendix.



\end{enumerate}



Subjects receive payments for their participants:
\begin{itemize}
    \item A base payment of \$20 and an average bonus of approx. \$10
    \item Bonus payment is calculated based on: (i) participants’ trading results at a rate of 200 experimental CASH units to \$1, (ii) forecasting ability (i.e. each price forecast that is within 2.5 units of actual price is rewarded with 5 CASH), (iii) a randomly chosen lottery that participants select from the experiment and (iv) the quiz result (subject receive \$0.25 for each of the 5 comprehension questions answered correctly.
\end{itemize}



Sample size:
We collected 19 markets with an average number of 18 subjects/market and hence 342 participants in total. In each market session, we collect biometric data from 3-5 in-lab participants. 


