\item[{\rm (b)}] In each of the remaining cases, the description of the relevant pairs $(A,B)$ is easier to state and it just depends on the subgroup $K$ of $H$ defined in part (ii) of the corollary. This subgroup $K$ is given in the relevant reference listed in the final column of Table \ref{tab:primary}, but for the reader's convenience we provide a brief description here:

