\noindent \textbf{Notation.} For a finite group $G$ and positive integer $n$, we write $C_n$, or just $n$, for a cyclic group of order $n$ and $G^n$ for the direct product of $n$ copies of $G$. An unspecified extension of $G$ by a group $H$ will be denoted by $G.H$; if the extension splits then we may write $G{:}H$. If $X$ is a subset of $G$, then we will write $i_2(X)$ for the number of involutions in $X$. And if $p$ is a prime, then ${\rm Syl}_p(G)$ is the set of Sylow $p$-subgroups of $G$. We will write $[n]$ for an unspecified soluble group of order $n$. Throughout the paper, we adopt the standard notation for simple groups of Lie type from \cite{KL} and we write $(a,b)$ for the highest common factor of the positive integers $a$ and $b$.

