    The VB detector converges quickly—typically within three iterations—even with five multipaths, indicating stable posterior estimates early on. In contrast, the MPA detector shows slower convergence and higher early residuals, especially in rich multipath channels, leading to BER saturation. Notably, MPA exhibits residual oscillation at $P=5$. While using maximum residuals helps overall convergence, it may cause large local errors and struggles more as multipaths increase. Overall, VB offers higher accuracy, faster convergence, and better robustness for complex, low-SNR conditions.
