\paragraph{Event builder}

The event builder is a transformer node responsible for taking the set of records passing the trigger threshold(s) and adding other records around them to form an acquisition that is likely to capture a full event (as shown in \autoref{fig:psyllid_event_builder_example}).  An acquisition includes a number of records before the acquisition is triggered, called the pre-trigger, and records to fill in small gaps between triggered records, called the skip tolerance.  Both the input and output data types to the event builder are trigger-flags.

\begin{figure*}[tb]
\centering  
\includegraphics[width=0.7\linewidth]{psyllid_event_builder_example.pdf}
